WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.601
- [Narrator] Once upon a time,
a war was about to happen.

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:04.640
The battle lines were drawn,

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:08.030
the soldiers were in
place, ready to fight.

00:00:08.030 --> 00:00:10.630
But a higher power made them stop,

00:00:10.630 --> 00:00:15.460
something unexpected and
delicious, a warm milk soup.

00:00:16.693 --> 00:00:19.360
♪ Ooh, ooh, ooh ♪

00:00:24.044 --> 00:00:24.877
(gentle music)

00:00:24.877 --> 00:00:25.840
- [Narrator] Our story starts here,

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:28.900
in the Swiss countryside
in Kappel am Albis,

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:30.710
where our special peacekeeper dish

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:33.120
was created almost five centuries ago.

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.350
Legend has it, actually
let's get Georg on the phone.

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.650
He's a historian from
the University of Basel

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:42.130
and he knows this milk soup so well,

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:45.037
he's even written articles about it.

00:01:24.310 --> 00:01:26.200
- [Narrator] After a while,
the soldiers got tired

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:29.000
and hungry so they put what
food they had together.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.540
The Catholics brought the milk,

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:32.690
and the Protestants the bread.

00:01:32.690 --> 00:01:35.766
And together they made
the legendary milk soup.

00:01:35.766 --> 00:01:37.581
♪ Hallelujah ♪

00:01:37.581 --> 00:01:39.487
♪ Hallelujah ♪

00:01:39.487 --> 00:01:44.487
♪ Hallelujah, hallelujah, hallelujah ♪

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:47.700
- [Narrator] This halted the
battle and a truce was formed.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:49.360
The soup became so iconic,

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.680
it has a memorial in the battlefield,

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:53.520
and nearly 500 years later,

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:55.703
the soup is still playing peacemaker.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.130
- [Narrator] And this is Robert,
whose restaurant has been

00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:01.051
serving the stuff for many years.

00:02:01.051 --> 00:02:03.634
(jaunty music)

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.640
- [Narrator] He makes
the soup the modern way,

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:18.500
with milk and bread of
course, but also with butter,

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:21.470
onions, leek, cream, vegetable stock,

00:02:21.470 --> 00:02:22.860
and some salt and pepper.

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:33.530
- [Narrator] So next time you're upset

00:02:33.530 --> 00:02:36.190
about something with your
neighbor, do as the Swiss do.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:38.760
You bring the bread,
have them bring the milk,

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.556
and have a bowl of soup together.

00:02:40.556 --> 00:02:42.973
♪ Hallelujah ♪

00:02:48.941 --> 00:02:52.274
(electronic tone pings)

